    "Left and right headers are each drawn as one continuous black strip but the pins have a spacing gap (left: after VIN; right: between ~D8 and D7). Transcribed as one connector per side; the gap may indicate two separate physical headers per side.",
    "Image 3 shows USB1 and USB2 connectors with individually labeled signals (+5V, USB D-, USB D+, USB ID, GND); not transcribed because physical pin positions are not shown."
  ],
  "notes": "Label = microcontroller port name (PA23...) where printed (rule 5 GPIO name); Arduino board names first in functions. Timer boxes containing two entries (e.g. \"TC4/WO[1] TCC0/WO[5]\") kept as one printed string. O/0 decided by context (TCC0, WO[0], SC0 digit zero; WO letter O). The AT32UC3A4256HHB internal port list in image 3 (PA02/PB22 etc.), LEDs, and the 6-20 V barrel jack are not header positions and were skipped."
}